# Project Logbook

**Project Title:** A Real-Time Chaotic Image Encryption Model on NVIDIA Jetson Nano

---

## Logbook Entry 1: Literature Review

**Date:** Week 1

**Objective:**
To study existing research on chaotic image encryption techniques and real-time embedded implementations.

**Activities Performed:**

* Reviewed IEEE and Springer papers on permutation–diffusion based chaotic encryption.
* Studied logistic, tent, and Henon chaotic maps.
* Analyzed prior work involving GPU and embedded platforms.

**Tools/Resources Used:**
IEEE Xplore, Google Scholar

**Outcome:**
Identified suitable chaotic models and performance gaps in existing real-time implementations.

---

## Logbook Entry 2: Chaotic Algorithm Selection

**Date:** Week 2

**Objective:**
To select and define an appropriate chaotic encryption algorithm for real-time execution.

**Activities Performed:**

* Compared different chaotic maps based on complexity and randomness.
* Designed permutation and diffusion stages.
* Defined key space and initial parameters.

**Tools/Resources Used:**
Research papers, mathematical simulations

**Outcome:**
Finalized a permutation–diffusion based chaotic encryption scheme using logistic and Henon maps.

---

## Logbook Entry 3: MATLAB Implementation

**Date:** Weeks 3–4

**Objective:**
To implement and validate the chaotic encryption algorithm in MATLAB.

**Activities Performed:**

* Implemented chaotic sequence generation.
* Developed image permutation and diffusion logic.
* Verified encryption correctness and reversibility.

**Tools/Resources Used:**
MATLAB

**Outcome:**
A functional chaotic image encryption algorithm validated through simulations.

---

## Logbook Entry 4: Jetson Nano Integration

**Date:** Weeks 5–6

**Objective:**
To port the algorithm to the NVIDIA Jetson Nano platform.

**Activities Performed:**

* Installed JetPack SDK and required libraries.
* Set up OpenCV and CUDA environment.
* Integrated image capture pipeline.

**Tools/Resources Used:**
NVIDIA Jetson Nano, JetPack SDK, OpenCV

**Outcome:**
Successful deployment of the basic encryption pipeline on Jetson Nano.

---

## Logbook Entry 5: CUDA Optimization

**Date:** Weeks 7–8

**Objective:**
To optimize the encryption algorithm for real-time GPU execution.

**Activities Performed:**

* Implemented CUDA kernels for permutation and diffusion.
* Optimized memory transfers and kernel configurations.
* Enabled maximum performance mode on Jetson Nano.

**Tools/Resources Used:**
CUDA Toolkit, cuRAND

**Outcome:**
Achieved significant speedup using GPU-centric processing.

---

## Logbook Entry 6: Performance Benchmarking

**Date:** Week 9

**Objective:**
To evaluate real-time performance and stability.

**Activities Performed:**

* Measured encryption latency per frame.
* Tested multiple image resolutions.
* Analyzed frame rate and resource utilization.

**Tools/Resources Used:**
CUDA profiler, OpenCV

**Outcome:**
Real-time encryption achieved up to 720p resolution at ≥30 FPS.

---

## Logbook Entry 7: Final Documentation

**Date:** Week 10

**Objective:**
To prepare final project documentation and results.

**Activities Performed:**

* Compiled project report and feasibility analysis.
* Prepared figures, tables, and performance results.
* Finalized IEEE paper draft.

**Tools/Resources Used:**
LaTeX, IEEE template

**Outcome:**
Completed and submitted final documentation.


